Z||000001||Leadfoot||06-20-2001||06:03 PM||||I don't think there is a difference.  Take a look at the Fiero store.  The same part number is used for 85-88.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-20-2001||08:18 PM||||The original manifolds have a heat stove for the thermac. GM did away with it in the recall. The new heat stove clamps to the pipe going down to the catalyst.<P>87-88 4 cyl doesn't use thermac and thus doesn't need the heat stove.||||reg||1
